&lt;sub&gt;7&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;11&lt;/sub&gt;) ∨ (in&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;3&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;) ∨ (in&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;11&lt;/sub&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;∨ (in&lt;sub&gt;6&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;8&lt;/sub&gt;) ) ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;12&lt;/sub&gt; ∧ in&lt;sub&gt;13&lt;/sub&gt;" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="2140" y="1100" width="620" height="80" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cmb_n" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=8;fontSize=10;strokeColor=#808080;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" value="Combined graph. The left branch is the print witness, the right branch zkTLS, and the middle is the case where both claims are assumed. Within each branch the record of the job file and the record of the logs come from the same source; either claim can be replaced by its assumption, in which case the match checker is not needed. Nodes with the same number are the same input, repeated to keep lines short; gates are labelled with the node they establish." vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1110" width="620" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cmb_lg0" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Assumption or verifier parameter&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;trusted input" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="700.0" y="1110.0" width="150" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cmb_lg1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;fontSize=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Attestation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;untrusted until verified" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="870.0" y="1110.0" width="150" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell><mxCell id="cmb_lg2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;s